{"slug":"max-points-on-a-line","title":"Most Points on One Line","topic":"hashing","difficulty":"hard","order":284,"tags":["hashing","hash-map","geometry","gcd"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"Count equal slopes from a fixed point","body":["Fix a point `P`. Every other point `Q` lies on a line through `P` with a direction given by `(dx, dy) = Q - P`. Two points `Q1` and `Q2` are on the **same line through `P`** exactly when their directions are parallel. To compare directions without decimals, divide `(dx, dy)` by `gcd(|dx|, |dy|)` (the greatest common divisor) and fix the sign so that `dx > 0`, or `dx = 0` and `dy > 0`. Equal reduced directions mean the same line.",{"code":"for each point P (index i):\n    count = {}\n    for each point Q after P:\n        dx, dy = Q.x - P.x, Q.y - P.y\n        g = gcd(abs(dx), abs(dy)); dx //= g; dy //= g\n        if dx < 0 or (dx == 0 and dy < 0): dx, dy = -dx, -dy\n        count[(dx, dy)] += 1\n    best = max(best, max(count.values()) + 1)       # + the point P itself"},"Looking only at the points after `P` is enough: the line through the best group was already counted from its first point. Floating point slopes are dangerous here (`1/3` is not exact); reduced integer pairs are exact keys."]},"statement":["Given `n` different points with integer coordinates, find the largest number of points that lie on one straight line."],"inputFormat":["The first line has `n`.","Each of the next `n` lines has the coordinates `x` and `y` of a point."],"outputFormat":["Print the largest number of points on one line."],"constraints":["1 <= n <= 700","-10^4 <= x, y <= 10^4","All points are different."],"examples":[{"input":"5\n1 1\n2 2\n3 3\n1 2\n2 1\n","output":"3\n","note":"The points (1,1), (2,2) and (3,3) are on one line."}],"hints":["Fix one point and look at the direction to every other point.","Reduce the direction by the gcd and fix its sign, so that parallel directions get the same key.","The best line through the fixed point has (largest count) + 1 points."],"starter":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\nn = int(input())\npts = [list(map(int, input().split())) for _ in range(n)]\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\n#include <unordered_map>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <cstdlib>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<vector<long long>> pts(n, vector<long long>(2));\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < 2; j++) {\n            cin >> pts[i][j];\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        long n = Long.parseLong(next());\n        long[][] pts = new long[(int) n][2];\n        for (int i = 0; i < pts.length; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < pts[i].length; j++) {\n                pts[i][j] = Long.parseLong(next());\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["From each point the other points are grouped by their reduced direction; the biggest group plus the point itself is the best line through that point."],"complexity":"Time O(n^2 log C) on average, space O(n).","code":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\nn = int(input())\npts = [list(map(int, input().split())) for _ in range(n)]\n\nfrom math import gcd\nbest = 1\nfor i in range(n):\n    count = {}\n    for j in range(i + 1, n):\n        dx = pts[j][0] - pts[i][0]\n        dy = pts[j][1] - pts[i][1]\n        g = gcd(abs(dx), abs(dy))\n        dx //= g\n        dy //= g\n        if dx < 0 or (dx == 0 and dy < 0):\n            dx, dy = -dx, -dy\n        count[(dx, dy)] = count.get((dx, dy), 0) + 1\n    if count:\n        best = max(best, max(count.values()) + 1)\nprint(best)\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\n#include <unordered_map>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <cstdlib>\nusing namespace std;\n\nlong long gcdOf(long long a, long long b) {\n    while (b != 0) {\n        long long t = a % b;\n        a = b;\n        b = t;\n    }\n    return a;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<vector<long long>> pts(n, vector<long long>(2));\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < 2; j++) {\n            cin >> pts[i][j];\n        }\n    }\n\n    int best = 1;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        unordered_map<long long, int> count;\n        for (int j = i + 1; j < n; j++) {\n            long long dx = pts[j][0] - pts[i][0], dy = pts[j][1] - pts[i][1];\n            long long g = gcdOf(llabs(dx), llabs(dy));\n            dx /= g;\n            dy /= g;\n            if (dx < 0 || (dx == 0 && dy < 0)) {\n                dx = -dx;\n                dy = -dy;\n            }\n            best = max(best, ++count[dx * 100000 + (dy + 50000)] + 1);\n        }\n    }\n    cout << best << \"\\n\";\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    static long gcdOf(long a, long b) {\n        while (b != 0) {\n            long t = a % b;\n            a = b;\n            b = t;\n        }\n        return a;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        long n = Long.parseLong(next());\n        long[][] pts = new long[(int) n][2];\n        for (int i = 0; i < pts.length; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < pts[i].length; j++) {\n                pts[i][j] = Long.parseLong(next());\n            }\n        }\n\n        int best = 1;\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            Map<Long, Integer> count = new HashMap<>();\n            for (int j = i + 1; j < n; j++) {\n                long dx = pts[j][0] - pts[i][0], dy = pts[j][1] - pts[i][1];\n                long g = gcdOf(Math.abs(dx), Math.abs(dy));\n                dx /= g;\n                dy /= g;\n                if (dx < 0 || (dx == 0 && dy < 0)) {\n                    dx = -dx;\n                    dy = -dy;\n                }\n                best = Math.max(best, count.merge(dx * 100000 + (dy + 50000), 1, Integer::sum) + 1);\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(best);\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"5\n1 1\n2 2\n3 3\n1 2\n2 1\n","output":"3\n"},{"input":"1\n0 0\n","output":"1\n"},{"input":"2\n0 0\n5 7\n","output":"2\n"},{"input":"4\n0 0\n1 1\n0 1\n1 0\n","output":"2\n"},{"input":"10\n2 3\n2 -3\n-1 4\n3 3\n-4 1\n1 4\n1 -3\n-3 1\n-2 1\n-4 -3\n","output":"3\n"},{"input":"100\n-1286 -9245\n5409 8478\n4889 6837\n2320 -6064\n-4190 -5765\n-4993 -8188\n9026 -1364\n-6700 -9327\n-4335 -867\n-6623 4675\n9103 -6951\n-619 -149\n-1445 9143\n-8187 -6204\n3173 8097\n710 6741\n4502 3766\n980 329\n3240 9389\n6839 -9476\n8121 -5687\n-524 -2013\n9977 6409\n3231 2656\n-3086 9584\n-6043 1852\n8244 -6456\n-2588 2452\n-4701 -4625\n8498 9578\n1137 -1114\n1814 -2284\n-1615 -1196\n3643 -5469\n7256 -4806\n-8463 5881\n138 -9974\n948 3258\n5365 1133\n-2852 -5069\n-209 5937\n8116 -1640\n-5651 8315\n232 -8064\n8332 8565\n-118 6165\n6581 -1810\n-8912 -3845\n-6254 6532\n-8771 4045